// Phase-0 spike mission: the smallest thing that boots on Stratis and exercises
// the shim. Superseded as the mission that is played by missions/cti.Stratis
// (ADR-0007), and kept — #165 decided this — because it still has consumers.
// Anything that walks missions/ has one here: `just build` packs every directory
// under it, and `just spike` boots this one, because it runs spike/run.sh with
// nothing overridden and run.sh's defaults are this mission and spike/server.cfg,
// whose Missions class names it in turn. Check there rather than trusting a list
// kept here. ADR-0011 retires the recipe and this world together when
// `just accept` arrives in Phase 3; deleting it before then breaks a live recipe,
// and git history holds it if #8 ever wants it back after that.
//
// Not a convenience world: `just probe` brings up the Phase-1 one. This mission
// is open by construction (the CfgRemoteExec note below), and the config that
// boots it lists the human's LAN address in localClient[] — #8's candidate
// cause 1, and the reason to reach for `just probe` unless the Phase-0
// measurements are the point.
briefingName = "arma-cti phase-0 spike";
onLoadName = "arma-cti phase-0 spike";
author = "arma-cti";

class Header
{
    gameType = "Coop";
    minPlayers = 1;
    maxPlayers = 2; // must equal the playable roles in mission.sqm (1 rifleman + 1 HC)
};

briefing = 0;
debriefing = 0;

respawn = "BASE";
respawnDelay = 5;
respawnDialog = 0;
disabledAI = 1;
joinUnassigned = 1;
enableDebugConsole = 1;

// No CfgRemoteExec here, deliberately (#115). The engine's default is mode 2 —
// "remote execution is fully allowed, ignoring the whitelist"
// (topics/Arma_3_CfgRemoteExec.wiki) — which the wiki keeps only for backward
// compatibility, so this mission lets any machine remote-execute anything, and
// the debug console above is open beside it. That is what a spike is: it boots
// on a local dedicated server on one person's own machine with no untrusted
// joiner, and the harness reaches into it on purpose. missions/cti.Stratis is
// the mission that is played, and it locks Functions and Commands to mode 1
// with the gateway whitelisted to target the server alone. Copying that block
// here would put a lock on scaffolding that Phase 3 deletes, and would say this
// mission had been thought about as a play surface. It has not: it is a
// laboratory, and this comment is the sign on the door.
